{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages","id":609097,"title":"Trans mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-31T01:57:42-07:00","id":609097,"title":"Trans mages","content":"Honestly I have nothing specific to say except just imagine a trans Mastigos talking over someone's explanation of Space increasingly loudly to correct 'real name' to 'sympathetic name'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T02:13:12-07:00","id":609132,"title":"","content":"Sympathy depends entirely on how important something is to you. If you value your new name enough, it can become your &quot;real&quot; name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T02:31:33-07:00","id":609175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=609132#post609132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sympathy depends entirely on how important something is to you. If you value your new name enough, it can become your &quot;real&quot; name.</div> </div> </div> </div>so you mean with enough self-love, I can truely Identify as an Attack Helicopter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4652-rising","name":"Rising","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4652_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:01:07-07:00","id":609221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=609132#post609132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sympathy depends entirely on how important something is to you. If you value your new name enough, it can become your &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually you can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:05:31-07:00","id":609227,"title":"","content":"Ok I will be open, I've always been alittle confused as to how this works.<br /> <br /> I am actually trans myself I transitioned nearly 10 years ago in my teens, Most people I know these days have never known me from before. As such my current name is the only name they know me by. Even those that do have mentioned that they don't really think of me as the same person I was back then understandably so because my personality was quite different.<br /> But I've heard different ideas about &quot;Real names&quot;<br /> It's what you truly identify as (Your name can change)<br /> It's what's intimate (It's changes but also stays the same)<br /> It's what the exarchs plan for you (Your name doesn't change)<br /> It's that first connection with the fallen (your name doesn't change)<br /> <br /> In my case I suppose I can understand the intimacy one, but I know the latter two are more common interpretations, because if you know my current name you know who I am now. If you know my old name aswell then you know who I was because presumably I'd have told you stories of my youth. But if you called me by my old name today I would look at you oddly then might be abit annoyed because I'd assume you were intentionally trying to be dense/insulting.<br /> <br /> I've never played a transgender mage (never felt the need to) But I have drawn upon those experiences of my early transition to play mages in general, Even when I was taking Hormones and I was changing both physically and psychologically There were different people who knew different things and it was important at the time to keep the worlds separate, what my family knew compared to what my classmates at collage knew vs what my friends knew and how it was important to keep these worlds apart lest disaster strike.<br /> <br /> I dunno what do you consider to be a &quot;Real name&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4641-pebbles","name":"Pebbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:16:37-07:00","id":609234,"title":"","content":"In Mage, at least as far as I remember, your True Name (assuming no archmage shenanigans) is the name you grew up with and used for a majority of your childhood. IIRC it isn't necessarily your birth name, but it is the name you first identified yourself as. Even if later on you change your name due to any sort of other life changes, as far as magic is concerned, that name you were raised by is your True Name. Whether you identify with it anymore or not is irrelevant, it is the name your soul first acknowledged as its own and will remain as such unless extremely powerful (imperial) magic is worked upon it to change that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:42:49-07:00","id":609242,"title":"","content":"Yeah; I think it's been made fairly repeatedly explicit that it doesn't matter what you think of as your name (or even if you <i>hate </i>your sympathetic name), by the time you're talking in complete sentences that ship has sailed. I just think it's a nice bit of bite to a trans mage's backstory (the idea that a name they most likely no longer identify with and may well hate is somehow more 'real') and also that you can only call sympathetic names real names so many times around the kind of bitter, militant queers i know and love and am before someone hexes you.<br /> <br /> I did also have a legacy rooted in transness &amp; trans history brewing but the more I wrote it the less I liked it. I should have another stab at one after 2e come out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:35:06-07:00","id":609280,"title":"","content":"All that being said, you can change your true name, but it's an act of Archmastery.<br /> <br /> If it was just emotional attachment that determined your true name then Mages would run into the problem of their shadow name becoming their true name with some level of frequency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:39:34-07:00","id":609282,"title":"","content":"It's the first identification in the Fallen, and it doesn't change.<br /> <br /> In second ed, we play up the idea of Shadow Names as elective identities a lot more, and note that when mages appear in the astral they take on their soul's self-image, which can be radically different to their physical bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:40:23-07:00","id":609283,"title":"","content":"Real names are also far less important, magically, than they were in first edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T06:05:36-07:00","id":609298,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I like the change, given the topic at hand, because it does seem like an interesting drama hook for a Mage to be stuck the rest of her life with a &quot;true&quot; name that she doesn't relate to anymore.<br /> <br /> Curiously I'm trans myself but until now still pretty comfortable with my given unmistakenly male name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T06:13:06-07:00","id":609308,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't the official True Name be whatever you carved on the watchtower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T06:25:18-07:00","id":609311,"title":"","content":"No. And for sympathy, it's a real name. Mage only uses &quot; True Name&quot; as the title if an archmastery spell that encrypts your sympathetic identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T06:42:03-07:00","id":609316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't the official True Name be whatever you carved on the watchtower?</div> </div> </div> </div> You probably can't consciously choose what you write on the Watchtower, and even if you could, there are example characters who signed the Watchtower with a bloody handprint; what exactly is their real name? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crabbadon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">just imagine a trans Mastigos talking over someone's explanation of Space increasingly loudly to correct 'real name' to 'sympathetic name'.</div> </div> </div> </div> .... No, I don't think I shall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T06:46:29-07:00","id":609326,"title":"","content":"Ah, right. I guess I was thinking of Changeling and/or Dresden Files. <br /> <br /> I think the thing is, the supernal doesn't really understand the concept of &quot;boy names&quot; and &quot;girl names&quot;. There's just a string of sounds attached to the collection of symbols that make up &quot;you&quot;. It doesn't really care whether the symbols for male or female are statistically more likely to be assigned to that particular string of sounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:29:55-07:00","id":609398,"title":"","content":"Names are significant for Sleepers as well. Probably also for vampires and werewolves and the like (which can add a bit of significance for how many of them won't go by their human names; hell, a lot of old vampires might not even remember them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:21:37-07:00","id":609470,"title":"","content":"Official game terminology:<br /> <br /> Real name - Name you identified with growing up. Doesn't change. Grants bonus for sympathetic magic.<br /> True name - Name that replaces your real name for the purposes of sympathetic magic. Granted to you by an archmage.<br /> <br /> Yes, I can see a trans mage deciding to call their &quot;real&quot; (game terminology) name their sympathetic name instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:57:27-07:00","id":610121,"title":"","content":"Real name? You mean your slave name. that's just a serial number printed on your soul by a bunch of god-wardens. Forget it. your shadow name that is the real you. you tell the universe that your name is holywood and agents will find their way to you. tell the universe your real name Mordred and well... you'll see.<br /> <br /> Incidentaly...<br /> <br /> I have some friends on who bat for the other team (seers) and they might have just the legacy for you... Crysalides. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (also I gotta say I'm a bit disappointed by some posts in this thread. <sup>Anyway.</sup>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","user":"Nurseninja","date":". 07-31-2015, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T17:39:07-07:00","id":610189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nurseninja</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real name? You mean your slave name. that's just a serial number printed on your soul by a bunch of god-wardens. Forget it.</div> </div> </div> </div> You know, I feel as though this (and similar sentiments regarding subjects other than Mage) kind of uncomfortably appropriates the concept and significance of slave names and the rejection thereof. Like, no bitter young mage, the name your parents gave you and raised you by does not originate from some kind of systematic dehumanization or forced integration on the part of Exarchs who found whatever culture your name happens to come from more palatable to address you by, and even apart from the technical inaccuracies it's kind of silly and a little bit offensive to equate your desire to be called Jetstream with Abiyoe's desire to be called by the name from when he lived for himself rather than by the Adam given to him by masters who would prefer he forget he was ever not a slave and become a proper civilized Christian and also Abiyoe is kind of hard to pronounce. (I feel as though this is a sentiment worth expressing whether or not Nurseninja was being ironic)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T18:44:01-07:00","id":610242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nurseninja</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The name given to you, the destiny given to you, the world given to you was created by people who would have you be a world of slaves, a world of pain and misery.</div> </div> </div> </div> This feels a lot like saying that the children of actual slaves who were given secret African names by their parents which they went by whenever possible were also still just given slave names because if your parent is a slave then they can only ever do things that contribute to the institution of slavery. Or something else, it just... doesn't hold up logically. The premise of the Lie does not mean that everything that happens in the world is terrible, and I literally cannot figure out how the names parents give to children has anything to do with it. The Lie hangs over the world, but there are plenty of things that have nothing to do with it. The closest thing tha game gets to expressing that kind of sentiment is put into the mouths of a reviled Mysterium heresy who worked with the Nazis for the sake of trying to kill as many people as possible. I mean, if Selling and Seer threads want to talk about mustache twirlers... (note: the Mysterium heresy whose name I can never remember actually does with a fully coherent and relatively reasonable basis for a belief that they should kill as many Sleepers as possible)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T19:17:06-07:00","id":610255,"title":"","content":"I feel like some potentially problematic associations around the phrase &quot;real name&quot; in this context can be solved if the word &quot;real&quot; is replaced with &quot;birth&quot;. I think there's some level of unpleasantness around an implication, no matter how unintentional, that the properly gendered name that a trans person takes is some how less real at some sort of metaphysical level than the incorrectly gendered one they were given at birth. Even if we can handwave it as being about something else entirely by talking about supernal sympathy and the locking in of symbols with names, it still feels kind of wrong in ways that are hard to describe.<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure I'd have been as bothered by this prior to having watched Sense8; specifically how Nomi's mother's uses her pre-transition name Michael as an attack on her identity. Thinking of a bunch of transphobic mages going &quot;yeah, but we can *prove* that whatever you may want to be calling yourself now, your *real* name is..&quot; is kind of disturbing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T20:10:23-07:00","id":610304,"title":"","content":"I think Eolirin's point is a valid one, but I do think it's worth pointing out that these &quot;real names&quot; or &quot;birth names&quot; are emphatically not a good thing <i>because </i>of the way sympathy works. It's not about the name that you <i>want </i>to be called by, it's the one with really strong association with you, desired or not.<br /> <br /> I don't know if they kept it this way in 2e, but I remember reading somewhere in 1e that if you go by a certain name (not necessarily a Shadow Name?) long enough, it can develop sympathy with you. Maybe that's influenced by your desire to identify with it or not. I think a description of that name being a shackle tying you to an identity which is not wholly of your own making is sort of in-keeping with it.<br /> <br /> I feel this dips into questionable territory, but considering what Mages can use your sympathetic name for, I don't think it's completely inappropriate that the symbolic act of violence that is willfully ignoring a trans person's identtiy could be a component of the usage of your name against you.<br /> <br /> That said, for groups that are still uncomfortable with it, I would just handwave it based on the idea that whatever name other people most strongly associate with you is the &quot;real name&quot; for the purpose of sympathetic casting, so if you've been identifying as Kallista when your assigned name is Keith, Kallista carries more sympathy with who you are as a person.<br /> <br /> That said, I also think this sort of thing could also step on the toes of the Shadow Name, which is honestly a nice way to claim an identity with your own agency as opposed to the one being used as an essential GPS tag/collar/tool of your destruction for any Mage that knows it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T20:24:36-07:00","id":610312,"title":"","content":"I personally allow social security numbers, DNA printouts and names given during certain religious ceremonies, such as a catholic confirmation to be true names, for reasons similar to what leet said, in my games, the more unique a name is to a person, the more &quot;true&quot; it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T05:01:46-07:00","id":610674,"title":"","content":"Shame about the de-emphasis of true name stuff in Mage. I was hoping for it to have <i>greater </i>impact than less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T08:45:01-07:00","id":610903,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear, my issue isn't so much with how real names work in Mage, because it's a horror setting, and the idea that your birth name is a shackle that can be used against you is perfectly cool. My issue is entirely with the fact that the book, in an out of character fashion, is giving implicit weight to the point of view that that birth name is some how more real and legitimate than the identity of the character through its use of the word 'real'. It's not a real name in any way that'd matter to a person's sense of identity, it's just the label they were given at birth. And I think conflating those concepts is problematic in the context of people who suffer the same sort of conflation around other aspects of their identity.<br /> <br /> It makes me uncomfortable, which is fine for the mechanic to do, it's a good way to explore that kind of identity issue and the prejudices around it, but it's less fine for the book's language choice to implicitly support that mentality even as it sets up the issue to be explored. Edit: to be super, super, clear, I do *not* think there is any intention to do that on the part of the writers, whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Also I don't think this is necessarily a huge deal or anything either, just something to perhaps consider, but I'm also not transgender, so I can't really speak to how big a deal this would be to someone who is.<br /> <br /> Edit: also, to be clear about the metaphysics, given the sorts of source material Mage draws on, the birth name being the thing that gets locked into place has strong thematic weight; names have power, and the idea that things without names are more malleable and unclaimed, and that naming them locks them into more static shapes and grants power over the thing being named is very much in keeping with a host of important inspirations for the line. Using other things or tying it to identity related things is obviously fine, as a choice by the ST, but it does abandon those thematic associations. I just think drawing a cleaner line between 'this is what naming a person who has no name does in the setting's metaphysics' and 'this has anything to do with a person's identity' is maybe worth looking at; this thread provides plenty of examples of people struggling with completely separating the two, when, metaphysically, they have nothing to do with each other, and I think the word choice 'real' is the core of that conflict. It's really just your birth name, the first name that was used to describe you. It's locked, it never changes, it's a name, and names have power. It's not your identity, it's not the core essence of you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","user":"Eolirin","date":". 08-01-2015, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T09:40:03-07:00","id":610933,"title":"","content":"I kind of agree that &quot;birth name&quot; or maybe &quot;child name&quot; is probably a better way to describe it, even if sometimes it's not the very first name you were given. My explanation to players that the reason it lends such potent sympathy isn't because it's tied to your identity, so much as because it is tied to your origin, your childhood. It gives someone power over you because they know the name you were called before you had the power and agency to name yourself. It lets them symbolically usurp the place of someone who has known you since you were a child. Or, alternatively, you voluntarily allow them to retroactively share such a place. I really liked the angst of how the protagonist of the Imperial Mysteries intro fiction was unable to share her legacy because she didn't know her own birth name. I don't remember if that's actually in the rules, but it suggests that the mentor-student relationship must be cemented through trust, symbolized by a ritual &quot;I wasn't always called The Nemean&quot; disclosure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T09:43:27-07:00","id":610934,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's a really good way of putting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:20:13-07:00","id":611270,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd rather just have it always be True Name rather than only having that be used in the context of archmage granted names. I don't mind archmages being able to change it, I just don't see a reason why it would then get a new name. That and I think True Name sounds cooler. As for whatever is more politically correct, I don't really care one way or the other, I'd just go with what sounds best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T15:33:06-07:00","id":611416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=611270#post611270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'd rather just have it always be True Name rather than only having that be used in the context of archmage granted names. I don't mind archmages being able to change it, I just don't see a reason why it would then get a new name. That and I think True Name sounds cooler. As for whatever is more politically correct, I don't really care one way or the other, I'd just go with what sounds best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. I'm not sure I can respond to that civilly, at least without being condescending. &quot;Political correctness&quot; really has not a thing to do with this conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T16:35:44-07:00","id":611447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=611416#post611416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. I'm not sure I can respond to that civilly, at least without being condescending. &quot;Political correctness&quot; really has not a thing to do with this conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well since these things tend to derail topics pretty hard would you prefer to discuss it privately? You can be as uncivil as you want there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T20:29:13-07:00","id":611761,"title":"","content":"True Name would be cooler than Real Name, and I agree it is kind of unnecessary to change how it is called just because an Archmage changed it.<br /> <br /> But I would stay with Sympathetic Name to start with, because all the reasons posited by Eolirin, <b><u>and</u></b> because it sounds more academic, so it is even cooler.<br /> <br /> I would personaly add in my chronicles that most Mages use True Name because it is short and cool, but it DOES raise some problems from Mages with issues about identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T20:45:14-07:00","id":611779,"title":"","content":"I did not get all the fuss with making &quot;Real Name&quot; and True Name. That Archmages can change it does not need the separated category. True Name is very profound occult term, one that is intrinsic to almost anyone remotely connected to magic. I, literally, had a lot of trouble to explain mine players that True =/= Real and in fan polish terminology of <b>Mage</b> we still have debate how to call both Names. I know that corebook is practically ended, but I would really like to rise this small, but a rather pervessive problem to solve in 2ED. I will make a topic for this.<br /> <br /> As to trans mages - I assume they affiliate much more with their Shadow Name persona. They want to run from True Name as much as they can - at least till the time when they can meet Archmage that can change it for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T21:17:13-07:00","id":611840,"title":"","content":"You know what? To the Lower Depths with silk gloves. I will be fully honest in this post. If you feel that my grievances do not apply to you, then please don't reply saying you were offended and that I should check my privilege. Nobody is forcing you to read this.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Please stop turning the subtext of entertainment into major political issues.</i></b><br /> <br /> Do LGBT+ people suffer because of their differences? Yes, absolutely. Do they have the same rights as non LBGT+ people? Yes, definitely. At the risk of sounding like a falsely apologetic bigot, let me say that I have a trans friend. I do not tolerate her existence, because the word &quot;tolerate&quot; implies her existence is wrong. She is my friend, and <i>that's it.</i><br /> <br /> The world, viewed as a Big Picture, does not give one particle of significance to your personal struggles. It is only when there is reunion and clear, reasonable goals that it makes a difference. There IS internal conflict and prejudice in the LGBT+ community. Founding a group/movement with noble intentions does not forever save it from bigotry if humans are supposed to join. Do you think I'm slandering? Simply do a quick Google search for &quot;tumblr hypocrisy&quot; or anything similar. The LGBT+ movement remains because there are still a lot of very stubborn people who dismiss or attack it without so much as one question asked.<br /> <br /> Am I somehow trying to sneak in a message that all LGBT+ people can only be physically affectionate where no one can see it and that they cannot mention their LGBT+ related experiences in public? <i><b>No, do not put such words into my mouth. </b></i>When I see a non heterosexual couple making out, I do my best to not turn that into an excuse for talking politics with someone who is bothered by the sight. My only problem is on the extremely rare but real scenario where said couple does it for attention and controversy fodder, rather than love. That is <i>messed up.<br /> <br /> <b>Yes, entertainment can be a political tool. </b></i>But you need to have common sense when deciding if a given piece of entertainment is worth discussing in regards to its possible undue influence on people's lives. Is &quot;Jackass&quot; a psychic virus meant to turn all those who watch it into an army of drooling puppets for [INSERT ANYTHING HERE]? No, just no. Do you wanna discuss works like Orwell's &quot;1984&quot; or Ayn Rand's &quot;Atlas Shrugged&quot;? By all means, go ahead and be mindful of <a href=\"http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/wheatons-law\" target=\"_blank\">Wheaton's Law.</a> Please don't try to convince me that all art is equal. Your chances of succeeding are microscopic. They are not 0% because I can change my mind with proper dialogue. All art is only equal in its right to exist, if other basic rights are being respected.<br /> <br /> You CAN include and address LGBT+ issues or any other type of prejudice in your TRPGs, bar chats or whatever. However, you should make it obvious that being part of one or more minority groups that have been mistreated for a long time is not the sum of the issues you care about. That would make you a willing caricature.<br /> <br /> This little soapbox o' mine could be a lot longer, but I feel like I made myself clear without aggression. I'll just leave a few last observations.<br /> <br /> Depicting is not synonymous with endorsing.<br /> <br /> You can and should fight for equality before the law, but don't expect universal and permanent acceptance on a cultural level.<br /> <br /> &quot;There is a time and a place&quot; doesn't mean you are being censored. &quot;Do not talk about this, or else&quot; is what censorship means.<br /> <br /> Lastly but not least, hidden agendas are not omnipresent.<br /> <br /> EDIT: regarding magical nomenclature, I would suggest calling the True Name the &quot;Birth Name&quot;, and keep Shadow Name as is. You can be okay with your Birth Name or not, neither are automatically wrong. The fact that jerk Mages can use your Birth Name which you don't like to both humiliate you and cast sympathetic spells on you is actually a plot hook if you think about it. You might be Jane now, but Jack did bad things when he was feeling alone and misunderstood. It's up to you and those who think you really deserve help to clear your reputation, so that said jerks will no longer want to Sympathetically Fray you. Or at least face heavy consequences for doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-02-2015, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T12:56:45-07:00","id":612520,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, your True Name is the name of your soul. That is to say that it is something beyond &quot;Mike&quot;, &quot;Samantha&quot;, or &quot;Bibembop&quot;, but it is the core identity of who you are and who you're meant to be. It CAN change, but it is very difficult to do so (requires you consciously choosing to be something other than &quot;yourself&quot;)<br /> <br /> As far as Mage is concerned, I think that means that everyone is born ignorant to their True Name. Yet some people, somehow, come to realize who they truly are, and their place in the Fallen World. This is what we think of as Awakening. At the end of your Awakening (be it Mystery Play or Shadow) you come to your watchtower, and have a choice. You can either 1) inscribe your True Name upon the Watchtower, accepting fully who you are and your soul's identity. OR you can 2) reject your True Name, and inscribe YOUR name (however you want to present yourself) on the Watchtower, which is what creates Banisters. (the reason they hate Magic is because, on some deep level, they envy those that could accept who they are, and are ashamed that they could not [or, scarier still, their True Name scared them shirtless]). This being said, Joining a Legacy is difficult because it DOES involve changing your True Name, and even more so for becoming an Archmaster.<br /> <br /> Those are just my immediate thoughts off the top of my head, so feel free to disagree/agree/question/whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1798-nameandverb","name":"NameAndVerb","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1798_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T13:45:42-07:00","id":612571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NameAndVerb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=612520#post612520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, your True Name is the name of your soul. That is to say that it is something beyond &quot;Mike&quot;, &quot;Samantha&quot;, or &quot;Bibembop&quot;, but it is the core identity of who you are and who you're meant to be. It CAN change, but it is very difficult to do so (requires you consciously choosing to be something other than &quot;yourself&quot;)<br /> <br /> As far as Mage is concerned, I think that means that everyone is born ignorant to their True Name. Yet some people, somehow, come to realize who they truly are, and their place in the Fallen World. This is what we think of as Awakening. At the end of your Awakening (be it Mystery Play or Shadow) you come to your watchtower, and have a choice. You can either 1) inscribe your True Name upon the Watchtower, accepting fully who you are and your soul's identity. OR you can 2) reject your True Name, and inscribe YOUR name (however you want to present yourself) on the Watchtower, which is what creates Banisters. (the reason they hate Magic is because, on some deep level, they envy those that could accept who they are, and are ashamed that they could not [or, scarier still, their True Name scared them shirtless]). This being said, Joining a Legacy is difficult because it DOES involve changing your True Name, and even more so for becoming an Archmaster.<br /> <br /> Those are just my immediate thoughts off the top of my head, so feel free to disagree/agree/question/whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like that explanation, though I would hesitate to make that the only way of ending up a Banisher. Now I think that True Name should be called Soul Name, since the latter term accepts the possibility of change, even if extremely difficult. I still think Shadow Name should remain just that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T14:11:18-07:00","id":612589,"title":"","content":"That's... not really an opinion. It's more of a headcanon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T14:57:18-07:00","id":612627,"title":"","content":"what even happened in this thread<br /> who is gottagofeast even <i>talking</i> to<br /> i guess i shoulda contributed more actively to this thread if i wanted a thread about trans mages, huh<br /> (trying to remember if there's any canonically trans mages in the existing books now. I've not cover-to-covered most of them, and I can't think of any just off the top of my head.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T15:11:00-07:00","id":612634,"title":"","content":"All I know is that Dave has made it a point to address how mages (and people in general?) in the Astral look like their image of themselves, with all that that implies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T16:12:57-07:00","id":612770,"title":"","content":"There's an entire Legacy of Mages that have very fluid sex and gender identities called the Daksha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T16:26:17-07:00","id":612775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crabbadon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=612627#post612627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what even happened in this thread<br /> who is gottagofeast even <i>talking</i> to<br /> i guess i shoulda contributed more actively to this thread if i wanted a thread about trans mages, huh<br /> (trying to remember if there's any canonically trans mages in the existing books now. I've not cover-to-covered most of them, and I can't think of any just off the top of my head.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Nobody in particular, but most certainly not to the walls. It was a rant, I admit it. It was prompted by thoughts that reminded me of outside baggage. I did not point at any user and call them names. I had enough restraint to speak plainly without breaking any forum rules. If it turns out that I am wrong, I will concede. You don't have to be hesitant about talking to me. I will not go into Death Rage.<br /> <br /> To keep the topic relatively on track, I'd say that since shapeshifting is a nigh universal power in the NWOD (the only monsters that can't shapeshift are the Kereberoi, if memory serves), the core conflict is not having your ideal body. You can trade some favors with a mentor that has the right Gifts/Arcana/Contracts etc and maintain your desired body in public. But the problem is that powers in the NWOD are almost always temporary in effect. Non Archmage uses of Life and Mind cannot permanently alter the Patterns of living beings and their identities. You can keep it up for along while, but your number of maximum active spells is capped by Gnosis + 3. And in 2ed, a flawless transition from one body to another might require Reach, and thus risk Paradox. Even if you overcome all magical obstacles, you still have to affirm your new self in a way that people recognize and respect. Not adore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-02-2015, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T16:50:40-07:00","id":612786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's an entire Legacy of Mages that have very fluid sex and gender identities called the Daksha. </div> </div> </div>They're not great examples. They're less about gender identity as such and more about what their idiosyncratic theosophy tells them they should become.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T17:00:13-07:00","id":612789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=612770#post612770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an entire Legacy of Mages that have very fluid sex and gender identities called the Daksha.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And the chrysalides from seers of the throne. their husk form and their inner form can be of diferent genders. in fact the body dysmorphia angle works even better if you were looking role play the complexities of trans living . <br /> <br /> On the angle of political correctness or bringing politics into games the following two videos I have found really educational.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=owEMDcq73IY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=owEMDcq73IY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=owEMDcq73IY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=owEMDcq73IY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7_tdztHiyiE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7_tdztHiyiE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7_tdztHiyiE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7_tdztHiyiE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> they are video game-centric but I think still relavant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T18:12:13-07:00","id":612870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nurseninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=612789#post612789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And the chrysalides from seers of the throne. their husk form and their inner form can be of diferent genders. in fact the body dysmorphia angle works even better if you were looking role play the complexities of trans living .<br /> <br /> On the angle of political correctness or bringing politics into games the following two videos I have found really educational.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=owEMDcq73IY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=owEMDcq73IY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=owEMDcq73IY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=owEMDcq73IY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7_tdztHiyiE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7_tdztHiyiE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7_tdztHiyiE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7_tdztHiyiE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> they are video game-centric but I think still relavant.</div> </div> </div> </div> I will be honest another time. I clicked on these links expecting patronizing speeches about how close minded I am. I contained my impulses to stop the videos and paid attention until the end. They have very good points. But I must insist that I emphasized the fact that entertainment can be political. It's bold and in italics, even. I do know that no art exists in a vacuum. Perhaps I should have added a personal rule of thumb for measuring reasonable investment in such discussions. So I will.<br /> <br /> &quot;The more a given work of art influences far-reaching decisions, the more it deserves discussion&quot;. You can discuss works with trivial influence on society, that's not a sin. If you asked me to define &quot;trivial&quot;, I'd call it &quot;something so unconvincing AND delirious in its messages that almost everyone dismisses it outright&quot;. Mein Kampf is delirious in the extreme, but it convinces many that it is reasonable, thus making it not trivial. Meanwhile, we have Time Cube. Twenty years from now, people will still be reading and discussing Mein Kampf. Time Cube? Not so much.<br /> <br /> I <i>really</i> should stop here. I got caught up in my rants enough as is. If anyone has qualms about anything I said, send me a private message and we can talk it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-02-2015, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T18:28:40-07:00","id":612872,"title":"","content":"I don't think those links were intended for just you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T05:12:08-07:00","id":613232,"title":"","content":"I think the question of whether or not the game intends to use its themes and precepts to support certain people would already be rather definitively settled by the whole Astral thing. When it comes to the magic of names, I feel as though even without the issue of people whose identities are other than they were perceived by the people who gave them those names, referring to it as a real name would be reductive, but also fitting as a term mages would use. I personally would find alternatives intended to be more technical being widely used to just not have the same feel, even if there are characters who would logically advocate for those alternatives. It's like the difference between Yantra and Instrument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T06:52:13-07:00","id":613313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=612770#post612770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an entire Legacy of Mages that have very fluid sex and gender identities called the Daksha.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Make your own non-cryptofascist genderbending Legacy, with blackjack and hookers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T08:15:16-07:00","id":613378,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a new way of looking it should be used. Changing your real name isn't something that, as a person, you can do off hand. It takes time and effort for that change to happen. You have to grow into the new name.<br /> <br /> You are trying to leave behind your mortal name (&quot;real name&quot;) and grow into a new name that fits the real you (&quot;shadow name&quot;). Does that work?<br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the entire name-thing is overblown in Mage. Either it needs to be relevant beyond Space magic, or you'll have a significant number of players who just don't care. Magically speaking, names are supposed to be a big deal. They're supposed to give you power over a person. That really doesn't happen, though, with the way Awakened magic is set up. I can't help but feel the entire thing is lacking, and feels forced. In my experience, the whole name thing has ended up as a minor part of the game, at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-03-2015, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T08:40:48-07:00","id":613391,"title":"","content":"Well, some things that used to be only significant for sympathetic magic (blood, hair, nail clippings) are now fairly useful yantras for all the Arcana, so perhaps ...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T10:38:35-07:00","id":613639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=613378#post613378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps a new way of looking it should be used. Changing your real name isn't something that, as a person, you can do off hand. It takes time and effort for that change to happen. You have to grow into the new name.<br /> <br /> You are trying to leave behind your mortal name (&quot;real name&quot;) and grow into a new name that fits the real you (&quot;shadow name&quot;). Does that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Shadow Name is supposed to minimize the threat of sympathetic magic and magic leaking into your mortal life, so I'd say &quot;no&quot;. Hell, having a different common name than your &quot;real&quot; name would be beneficial, making it harder for your enemies to discover it by accident.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, I think the entire name-thing is overblown in Mage. Either it needs to be relevant beyond Space magic, or you'll have a significant number of players who just don't care. Magically speaking, names are supposed to be a big deal. They're supposed to give you power over a person. That really doesn't happen, though, with the way Awakened magic is set up. I can't help but feel the entire thing is lacking, and feels forced. In my experience, the whole name thing has ended up as a minor part of the game, at best. </div> </div> </div>&quot;It's easier for me to nuke you from the other side of the world&quot; isn't exciting enough for you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T17:45:25-07:00","id":614327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rising</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=609175#post609175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> so you mean with enough self-love, I can truely Identify as an Attack Helicopter?</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This directly references a very demeaning transphobic meme. I'll give the benefit of the doubt that it was meant to be a harmless throwaway joke</span>\u200b, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">but it isn't, and it isn't acceptable on these forums</span>. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is the first and only warning I'm giving\u200b, any other &quot;jokes&quot; like this will be met with suspensions.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T19:30:05-07:00","id":614412,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would like to see things change in Mage 2nd so that a transgender character could have his post-transition name be considered a true name, with all of the sympathetic vulnerabilities that come with it.<br /> <br /> The situation becomes a bit hairier when it comes to learning a transgender person's pre-transition name, and whether that should provide supernal sympathy or not. I know that transgender people often have their pre-transition names used by disapproving family members and acquaintances, and can only imagine how irritating and frustrating that must be. This could be a real-life example of a name being used as a weapon against a person, which is really what the whole True Name thing is all about. So I could see reasons to make it go either way... and I would like to see the game respect both choices.<br /> <br /> One thought I had was that perhaps among mages there is a &quot;shadow name ritual&quot; that a mage can do to erase their supernal sympathy to a name. Just calling yourself &quot;Arctos&quot; may work for a while, but after a while people will start thinking of you as &quot;Arctos&quot; and this could slowly become a new True Name for you. So to prevent this, they perform a shadow name ritual to break this sympathy. However, this ritual demands a name be presented as a True Name, and this name must already have a supernal sympathy to you. (So no, you cannot present a series of unintelligible syllables as your True Name) If you don't have one, the ritual will fail. The supernal demands that you have a name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","user":"Froggy711","date":". 08-03-2015, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T19:47:27-07:00","id":614433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=614412#post614412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I would like to see things change in Mage 2nd so that a transgender character could have his post-transition name be considered a true name, with all of the sympathetic vulnerabilities that come with it.<br /> <br /> The situation becomes a bit hairier when it comes to learning a transgender person's pre-transition name, and whether that should provide supernal sympathy or not. I know that transgender people often have their pre-transition names used by disapproving family members and acquaintances, and can only imagine how irritating and frustrating that must be. This could be a real-life example of a name being used as a weapon against a person, which is really what the whole True Name thing is all about. So I could see reasons to make it go either way... and I would like to see the game respect both choices.<br /> <br /> One thought I had was that perhaps among mages there is a &quot;shadow name ritual&quot; that a mage can do to erase their supernal sympathy to a name. Just calling yourself &quot;Arctos&quot; may work for a while, but after a while people will start thinking of you as &quot;Arctos&quot; and this could slowly become a new True Name for you. So to prevent this, they perform a shadow name ritual to break this sympathy. However, this ritual demands a name be presented as a True Name, and this name must already have a supernal sympathy to you. (So no, you cannot present a series of unintelligible syllables as your True Name) If you don't have one, the ritual will fail. The supernal demands that you have a name.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe the problem with such an approach is that it opens the door to being able to change true / real names without archmastery, with all the inherent problems and conflicts. The name is not about what a mage wants, feels they deserve, or believes if fair, it was simply about how they were identified upon their arrival into the Fallen World. As others have indicated, the shadow name reflects a mages identify and can change as circumstances dictate. Moreover, creating a transgender or related exception seems inconsistent and unnecessary in a setting where mages can alter their physical forms and minds (and a great deal more) with moderate proficiency in certain Arcana.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T21:21:15-07:00","id":614516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=614433#post614433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I believe the problem with such an approach is that it opens the door to being able to change true / real names without archmastery, with all the inherent problems and conflicts. </div> </div> </div> </div>1. The proposed ritual protects a name from gaining sympathy, it does not alter sympathy. I opened no such door.<br /> <br /> 2. I didn't even name arcana requirements for this ritual. If you would like to comment on what arcana requirements this would be, feel free.<br /> <br /> 3. Is there anything about this that couldn't already be done within the rules of the game, as they are now?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T22:13:53-07:00","id":614586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=614516#post614516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. The proposed ritual protects a name from gaining sympathy, it does not alter sympathy. I opened no such door.<br /> <br /> 2. I didn't even name arcana requirements for this ritual. If you would like to comment on what arcana requirements this would be, feel free.<br /> <br /> 3. Is there anything about this that couldn't already be done within the rules of the game, as they are now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave has already indicated, including earlier in this thread, that it requires archmastery to change a true name. This is exactly as it was in the current edition.<br /> <br /> A mage may generally reduce (or enhance) sympathetic connections with the Space Arcana (See, e.g., <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/paradoxical/\" target=\"_blank\">Reach and Paradox spoiler</a>), and by default it is far more difficult to cast sympathetic magic without knowledge of a subject's actual name, but in 1e and thus far spoiled in 2e, a mage's true name is its &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=609282#post609282\">first identification in the Fallen, and it doesn't change.&quot;</a> The desires or current identity of the mage are irrelevant.<br /> <br /> As I indicated in my post, I am quite comfortable with the current rule, and believe it maintains setting integrity, consistency and verisimilitude. If a character could change a true name without archmastery, it defeats the very purpose of the true name. Of course, you may run your games however you wish, and I certainly have no intention, desire or ability to try to force you to follow any rule you do not like or offends you or your players.<br /> <br /> Edit: If you want a name-changing ritual in your games, I would suggest that it require a minimum Space 5, with possible additional Death and Prime to alter the mage's soul and supernal connection, respectively. Anything much easier effectively obviates the true name mechanic, and it would probably just be easier to ignore the rule entirely. Alternatively, you might want to consider allowing the mage to purchase sufficient Allies. Mentor or other merits representing contacts with a relevant (and powerful) archmaster who had the ability to change a true name with Imperial Arcana. That would provide the name change that you seek as well as a great deal of role-playing opportunities due to debts owed to or interference of the archmaster in your character's life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 08-04-2015, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T01:06:38-07:00","id":614710,"title":"","content":"I can see the argument for there being unfortunate implications to the game design angle that sympathetic names work this way, and being called real names, but I don't really take issue with it. It's part of what makes the name-stuff tick, and as has been chewed over above, it's hard to make it easier to change, and there's always going to be elements that might make a player uncomfortable and have to be tweaked","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3204,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","user":"crabbadon","date":".  holy run on sentence batman 08-04-2015, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T03:01:49-07:00","id":614753,"title":"","content":"If your name could be changed depending on the emotional connections that govern sympathy there's every chance you would get stuck with the name you hate more than the name you've chosen to identify yourself by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T03:53:40-07:00","id":614780,"title":"","content":"The most annoying thing, in my opinion, about the so-called &quot;real names&quot; is that assuming its a birth name makes no sense when you're talking about sympathetic magic. A child is born under one name, gets adopted while still young, gets a new name (even if its just a different surname) before he knows his original one. <br /> <br /> Suddenly, the sympathetic magic latches onto some name that he's got a chance of never hearing before and doesn't relate too? All the sympathetic connctions our theoretical boy has involves the Ward family, and not the Jane Doe (died of drug OD) or the unknown birth father. <br /> <br /> Its not even just trans mages that theoretically have unfortunate implications here. Its any number of people. I get married and my name changes. My new name isn't real? I find that mildly disturbing. <br /> <br /> I get that its probably trying to keep it simple, but its clear that one size does NOT fit all. In fact, its blindingly obvious that we're not talking about one minority group here where the assumption of birthnames = &quot;real&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T04:03:21-07:00","id":614817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=613639#post613639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Shadow Name is supposed to minimize the threat of sympathetic magic and magic leaking into your mortal life, so I'd say &quot;no&quot;. Hell, having a different common name than your &quot;real&quot; name would be beneficial, making it harder for your enemies to discover it by accident.</div> </div> </div> </div> in 1e, sure. Dave said some stuff about the naming conventions change for 2e, and that names were less important. Plus, I'm trying to devise a new way of looking at the issue, not just have the old regurgitated. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;It's easier for me to nuke you from the other side of the world&quot; isn't exciting enough for you? </div> </div> </div> oh, please. That tired old claim is unrealistic. You open a window, you open yourself to being killed right back. Two way street, and all. So, no. Not exciting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T04:04:11-07:00","id":614819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=614780#post614780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most annoying thing, in my opinion, about the so-called &quot;real names&quot; is that assuming its a birth name makes no sense when you're talking about sympathetic magic. A child is born under one name, gets adopted while still young, gets a new name (even if its just a different surname) before he knows his original one.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, the sympathetic magic latches onto some name that he's got a chance of never hearing before and doesn't relate too? All the sympathetic connctions our theoretical boy has involves the Ward family, and not the Jane Doe (died of drug OD) or the unknown birth father.<br /> <br /> Its not even just trans mages that theoretically have unfortunate implications here. Its any number of people. I get married and my name changes. My new name isn't real? I find that mildly disturbing.<br /> <br /> I get that its probably trying to keep it simple, but its clear that one size does NOT fit all. In fact, its blindingly obvious that we're not talking about one minority group here where the assumption of birthnames = &quot;real&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The purported problems you discuss, IMHO, are a feature and not a bug in terms of role-playing opportunities.<br /> <br /> In fact, I would suggest you read the opening fiction to Imperial Mysteries, aptly entitled &quot;Names.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T04:08:41-07:00","id":614822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=614819#post614819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The purported problems you discuss, IMHO, are a feature and not a bug in terms of role-playing opportunities.<br /> <br /> In fact, I would suggest you read the opening fiction to Imperial Mysteries, aptly entitled &quot;Names.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> which is why I proposed a new way of looking at the entire thing. And promptly was shouted down. I do not accept the idea of a static name.<br /> <br /> EDIT - and, in the case of an adopted kid, still doesn't make sense. He's a kid, not someone on a quest. I think that birth=real is just a bad rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-04-2015, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T04:18:32-07:00","id":614838,"title":"","content":"I, personally, like the fact that once your soul recognizes its own name that it becomes pretty much impossible to change that and make it acknowledge a new one. It's the entire naming something gives you power over it shtick, and having the ability to casually change that name seems highly inappropriate to me. Regardless of what sort of advantage knowing somethings name gives, I really like how permanent it is. Even if you completely reinvent yourself as something completely different your soul will always recognize itself by the first name it truly knew, and that feels really meaningful to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T04:34:29-07:00","id":614851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=614822#post614822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> which is why I proposed a new way of looking at the entire thing. And promptly was shouted down. I do not accept the idea of a static name.<br /> <br /> EDIT - and, in the case of an adopted kid, still doesn't make sense. He's a kid, not someone on a quest. I think that birth=real is just a bad rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are certainly entitled to your opinions and can adjust the rules to suit your style and preferences. However, the concept and understanding of true names, and the perceived power behind the act of naming and names themselves, is well established in folklore and literature, and Mage is not really breaking any new ground in this area, despite your misgivings. <br /> <br /> Moreover, just because a rule may create perceived difficulties or obstacles for specific character ideas does not mean it's necessarily a bad or ineffective rule. The fact that you admittedly have received such push-back makes this more than evident. In fact, although numerous problems and areas of improvement for Mage 1e have been discussed over the years, I do not recall true names ever being a major source of consternation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/True_name\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/True_name\" target=\"_blank\"> True name - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/True_name\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/True_name </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/IKnowYourTrueName\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...owYourTrueName</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T05:35:39-07:00","id":614904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=614817#post614817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh, please. That tired old claim is unrealistic. You open a window, you open yourself to being killed right back. Two way street, and all. So, no. Not exciting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got corrected on this not too long ago, it's actually a lot less of a two way street than you imply. The person targeting you may have a stronger connection to you than you have to him, and you may not even get the chance to fire back if he's set up his spell to take you out from the get-go since Mage spells form in the mind and there's no discernible build-up of power before it goes off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T13:44:46-07:00","id":615512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=614851#post614851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, just because a rule may create perceived difficulties or obstacles for specific character ideas does not mean it's necessarily a bad or ineffective rule. The fact that you admittedly have received such push-back makes this more than evident. In fact, although numerous problems and areas of improvement for Mage 1e have been discussed over the years, I do not recall true names ever being a major source of consternation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/True_name\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/True_name\" target=\"_blank\"> True name - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/True_name\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/True_name </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/IKnowYourTrueName\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...owYourTrueName</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The concept maybe not, but game terms Real/True Names are unncesery repetition of idea and leads to confussion in using it. Why not just call this all True Name, and say that Archmasters can only change it? The we end with only two Names ( True and Shadow), not three - especially, as Real and True made <b>exactly</b> the same thing, only that True was granted to you by Archmaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T13:59:11-07:00","id":615522,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it's only a distinction that came up in the course of this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T14:01:26-07:00","id":615527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=615512#post615512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The concept maybe not, but game terms Real/True Names are unncesery repetition of idea and leads to confussion in using it. Why not just call this all True Name, and say that Archmasters can only change it? The we end with only two Names ( True and Shadow), not three - especially, as Real and True made <b>exactly</b> the same thing, only that True was granted to you by Archmaster.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would have no objection to simplifying the name terminology. I simply believe the basic rules concerning names are consistent with history and mythology, straightforward, and don't require modification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T14:18:19-07:00","id":615534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=615522#post615522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure it's only a distinction that came up in the course of this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehem, 1ED rulebook definition of Shadow Name in Lexicon:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw 1ED</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">shadow name: The moniker a mage adopts to hide his <b>real name </b>from mages who would use sympathetic magic against him or threaten his Sleeper friends and family.</div> </div> </div> </div>And whole Sympathy section that all the time states &quot;real name&quot;. Also, NPCs in official wirte up have Real Name, not the True Name.<br /> <br /> And in <b>Tome of Mysteries</b>...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tome of Mysteries</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>True Names</b><br /> Mages customarily take shadow names to confound sympathetic spells. But this kind of elementary precaution won\u2019t stop a powerful, determined enemy. Archmasters acquire a so-called True Name for extra protection. Of all the imperial spells, True Names are perhaps the best known. Archmages sometimes give their agents temporary True Names to guard them during their missions, and a permanent True Name is a potent boon. As Invisible Masters have given other willworkers True Names in the past, this is one of the better documented Imperial spells.<br /> <br /> The Imago and Practice used are still unknown, but the True Name has several properties: It replaces the subject\u2019s birth name for the purpose of casting sympathetic spells (the birth name is no more potent than a shadow name), and no known spell can forcibly steal the True Name from the subject\u2019s mind or make her forget it. Regardless of who granted it, it the True Name is, by default, only known to its owner. A mage with a True Name may tell another mage what it is, but never does so lightly.<br /> <br /> Mages theorize that a True Name rewrites the name on the recipient\u2019s Watchtower, but as archmages have reputedly given True Names to Sleepers, other supernatural entities and even objects, this does not appear to be a<br /> complete explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>And <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imperial Mysteries</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>True Name</b> (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022)<br /> The archmaster may remove the capacity of the spell\u2019s recipient to be targeted by sympathetic magic.<br /> Duration: Lasting<br /> The target of True Name counts as \u201cunknown\u201d to any sympathetic-range spells, even if the caster of those spells knows her real name. The ability of archmages and some other beings to regard \u201cunknown\u201d as \u201cdescribed\u201d still applies, but the degree of sympathy cannot be raised higher than that by any means.</div> </div> </div> </div>The phrases &quot;so-called True Name&quot; and pointing to &quot;real name&quot; as other things makes that there is in 1ED distinction on Real/True Name terms - and it's totally unnecessary. Just point that character has True Name from his childhood and Archmasters can change it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T17:20:22-07:00","id":615781,"title":"","content":"It looks like the True Name might not actually be a name at all. In fact, 7 dots is the practice of Excision isn't it? Plus the spell description clearly states that it's removing the ability to be affected Sympathetically, not granting a name at all. So what really seems to have happened here is some confusion from the name of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:45:31-07:00","id":616065,"title":"","content":"It's weird, I never considered a True Name to be &quot;True&quot; and therefore unchangeable because someone gave it to you or by some law of a Narcissistic universe; I figured it was because you responded to it an extremely formative state and capable of identifying with it seemlessly because you had no predisposition as to what &quot;Your Name&quot; was meant to be beyond the entity that is &quot;Self&quot; which in its on way made it Sublime. I think its only in later years that &quot;True Names&quot; lose there value. In my games I house rule the &quot;Truth&quot; of &quot;True Names&quot; and make it more of what you identified with more so than what was on a birth record. Example: my RL daughter's name is Kalista, but if she was seeking her &quot;True Name&quot; it would be &quot;Little Bit&quot; since that's what me and my ex-wife called her throughout her childhood. Only after being introduced to the prejudices of the big ugly world does a person lose value in their &quot;Name/Identity&quot; which isn't to say it wasn't true, just tainted by alien ideologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6516-mefathiel8","name":"mefathiel8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T11:55:06-07:00","id":617904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=614838#post614838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, personally, like the fact that once your soul recognizes its own name that it becomes pretty much impossible to change that and make it acknowledge a new one. It's the entire naming something gives you power over it shtick, and having the ability to casually change that name seems highly inappropriate to me. Regardless of what sort of advantage knowing somethings name gives, I really like how permanent it is. Even if you completely reinvent yourself as something completely different your soul will always recognize itself by the first name it truly knew, and that feels really meaningful to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly why it's so problematic for trans people, though. So just because when Janet was born, her parents saw that she had a penis and said &quot;This looks like a boy. Let's call him Dave&quot;, this is now the designation that her soul recognizes? What does that even mean? When every fiber of her being screams at her &quot;this name is not who you are!&quot;, somehow her soul disagrees with her on that point? It stubbornly says &quot;nope, that's what your parents decided to call you, that must be my official designation.&quot; What is it about the parents decision to name the child that makes it so important? Shouldn't the person be the best authority on what title their own soul acknowledges for itself?<br /> <br /> I'm actually fine with the idea of a person's &quot;real&quot; name being locked in from early in life, as long as the determining factor is the person recognizing that name as their own, not just their parents choosing it. The first time that you realized the sounds the people around you kept making were referring to you, the first time you could put a word to your concept of self, the first name you identified with, if only on a basic level, that should be your &quot;real&quot; name, not the name on your birth certificate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T12:31:11-07:00","id":617925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=617904#post617904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's exactly why it's so problematic for trans people, though. So just because when Janet was born, her parents saw that she had a penis and said &quot;This looks like a boy. Let's call him Dave&quot;, this is now the designation that her soul recognizes? What does that even mean? When every fiber of her being screams at her &quot;this name is not who you are!&quot;, somehow her soul disagrees with her on that point?<i><b> It stubbornly says &quot;nope, that's what your parents decided to call you, that must be my official designation.&quot; What is it about the parents decision to name the child that makes it so important? Shouldn't the person be the best authority on what title their own soul acknowledges for itself?</b></i><br /> <br /> I'm actually fine with the idea of a person's &quot;real&quot; name being locked in from early in life, as long as the determining factor is the person recognizing that name as their own, not just their parents choosing it. The first time that you realized the sounds the people around you kept making were referring to you, the first time you could put a word to your concept of self, the first name you identified with, if only on a basic level, that should be your &quot;real&quot; name, not the name on your birth certificate.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=614851#post614851\">As indicated earlier</a>, the act of naming is a powerful and controlling force, often part of creation itself, it often has nothing to do with what the subject actually wants or believes, and is consistent with much of the body of established literature and myth concerning names. The shadow name is what reflects a character's identity, and the real name simply is a mage's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=609282#post609282\">first identification in the Fallen World</a>, no more, no less. The issues you describe are also a potentially plentiful source of role-playing opportunities. For instance, read the opening fiction to Imperial Mysteries, aptly entitled &quot;Names.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I understand how the concept, no matter how well established, may be uncomfortable for some people. If that's the case, either permit a change of the character's real/true name as part of the chronicle or character backstory (i.e., some involvement by an archmaster or significant power) or simply modify the rule to suit your preferences. I don't, however, believe the game needs to change a default, well-established, and fairly fundamental, mechanic that is consistent with real world mysticism.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 08-06-2015, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T12:33:13-07:00","id":617926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=617904#post617904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's exactly why it's so problematic for trans people, though. So just because when Janet was born, her parents saw that she had a penis and said &quot;This looks like a boy. Let's call him Dave&quot;, this is now the designation that her soul recognizes? What does that even mean? When every fiber of her being screams at her &quot;this name is not who you are!&quot;, somehow her soul disagrees with her on that point? It stubbornly says &quot;nope, that's what your parents decided to call you, that must be my official designation.&quot; What is it about the parents decision to name the child that makes it so important? Shouldn't the person be the best authority on what title their own soul acknowledges for itself?<br /> <br /> I'm actually fine with the idea of a person's &quot;real&quot; name being locked in from early in life, as long as the determining factor is the person recognizing that name as their own, not just their parents choosing it. The first time that you realized the sounds the people around you kept making were referring to you, the first time you could put a word to your concept of self, the first name you identified with, if only on a basic level, that should be your &quot;real&quot; name, not the name on your birth certificate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Theoretically, you could call the &quot;real&quot; name the &quot;assigned&quot; name. It's not something intrinsic to your soul - it's the Lie exerting influence on you. You were assigned this name, and in recognizing it, you tied yourself to it. You might hate it, or change it, or anything, but for the purposes of sympathetic magic, it's locked down.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5408-fetfet","name":"fetfet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5408_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T12:57:55-07:00","id":617944,"title":"","content":"I ways kinda figured that the True Name thing worked alittle like a computer. When a sympathetic spell is cast, the spell is given a name that that spell-action is to target. A file it searches for, so to speak. Lets say that that file is called &quot;Krobeles&quot;. To aid it in its search, it looks up other reference to &quot;Krobeles&quot; and finds relatively few and/or incorrect referances, because most of the people I interact with on a daily basis dont know that I use &quot;Krobeles&quot; as my internet handle. If you'de used my real name on the other hand, multiple references would pop up because I am associated with more of those referances.<br /> So in this fashion, a person would be able to change their &quot;True Name&quot; with time, but it would require that most of the reference that refers to the character by their old name, start associating the character with their new name.<br /> I am speaking from a strictly 1ed perspective here, since I haven't bothered keeping up with all the spoiler stuff regarding 2ed.<br /> <br /> I dont really see it as an issue, that its hard to change, and I find the complaints with regards to sensitivity towards transgender people extraordinarily silly. Its a pretty big deal to have your real gender/name changed. Why shouldn't it be a big deal to have your magical gender/name changed?<br /> Even if the writers came out and outright stated that its impossible to have it changed - which I am sure they wont - I'de consider that perfectly fine aswell. It was considered impossible to swap genders like a hundred years ago aswell. That seems like a pretty neat basis for a story, to uncover the way to change ones True Name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T13:41:34-07:00","id":618031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=617925#post617925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=614851#post614851\">As indicated earlier</a>, the act of naming is a powerful force and controlling force, often part of creation itself, it often has nothing to do with what the subject actually wants or believes, and is consistent with much of the body of established literature and myth concerning names. The shadow name is what reflects a character's identity, and the real name simply is a mage's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=609282#post609282\">first identification in the Fallen World</a>, no more, no less. The issues you describe are also a potentially plentiful source of role-playing opportunities. For instance, read the opening fiction to Imperial Mysteries, aptly entitled &quot;Names.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I understand how the concept, no matter how well established, may be uncomfortable for some people. If that's the case, either permit a change of the character's real/true name as part of the chronicle or character backstory (i.e., some involvement by an archmaster or significant power) or simply modify the rule to suit your preferences. I don't, however, believe the game needs to change a default, well-established, and fairly fundamental, mechanic that is consistent with real world mysticism.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And that sums up what I was going to say rather nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T14:03:54-07:00","id":618057,"title":"","content":"Skipping back on the forums with an unsettling note:<br /> <br /> Approximately 3 out of 5 Mages don't have the same worries about being trans (or hell, any sort of other self-identity issue, really.)<br /> <br /> An Obrimos can use Prime to make it <i>intuitively obvious</i> what gender they are, regardless of how much their fleshy shells might seem to disagree. And this would pretty much cover it for a lot of transgender people, I would think (it would obviously be insufficient for transsexuals.)<br /> <br /> Thyrsus are <i>really obvious</i>.<br /> <br /> And Mastigos? Dear lord, Mastigos. I don't think it would take Space 5 to change your True Name, it would just involve being willing to maintain a proper Veiling (heck, one of the spoiled spells let you wipe all your sympathetic connections, so it isn't like they are sacrosanct.) As for Mind...<br /> <br /> Any Mage who is sufficiently good at Mind can wake up in the morning and decide to try out being gay that day. Or straight. Or a bigot, Or a member of this or that social group. Heck, it's a path to personal growth, if you think about it - walk a thousand miles in someone else's shoes, and all that.<br /> <br /> Their gender doesn't match their fleshy shell, and they don't have the Life to change it? Just change your gender. As far as you are concerned, the problem is solved. Prime might also be able to pull this off... maybe.<br /> <hr /><br /> Acanthus and Moros are kinda out of luck though (I dunno - maybe Fate could streamline the whole transitioning process with <i>amazing</i> luck. But I can't see a way to use Death or Matter in an appropriate way). But otherwise...<br /> <br /> Unlike the proverbial physician, Mages <i>can</i> heal themselves. So I'd assume that any Mage that didn't address the issue has a good reason for doing so.<br /> <br /> Now, the Hubris of doing so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:17:22-07:00","id":618504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=610312#post610312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally allow social security numbers, DNA printouts and names given during certain religious ceremonies, such as a catholic confirmation to be true names, for reasons similar to what leet said, in my games, the more unique a name is to a person, the more &quot;true&quot; it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't like any Mage beyond a neonate have several mundane identities and driver's licenses, or social security numbers right? Just ask your Obrimos Jesus girl to fix you right up if you don't have some computer knowledge and Forces 2-3 worst case scenario.<br /> <br /> In Mage the Ascension the VA's only saw one side of the coin. Information is in fact free but they never grasped it can both be altered or totally controlled depending on your actual goal/goals.<br /> <br /> Given this is Mage the Awakening and both in game and out there is an objective truth wouldn't you be friends with some person that knows a bit about identity and how to spoof technology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 08-07-2015, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T01:57:36-07:00","id":618639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=618057#post618057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skipping back on the forums with an unsettling note:<br /> <br /> Approximately 3 out of 5 Mages don't have the same worries about being trans (or hell, any sort of other self-identity issue, really.)<br /> <br /> An Obrimos can use Prime to make it <i>intuitively obvious</i> what gender they are, regardless of how much their fleshy shells might seem to disagree. And this would pretty much cover it for a lot of transgender people, I would think (it would obviously be insufficient for transsexuals.)<br /> <br /> Thyrsus are <i>really obvious</i>.<br /> <br /> And Mastigos? Dear lord, Mastigos. I don't think it would take Space 5 to change your True Name, it would just involve being willing to maintain a proper Veiling (heck, one of the spoiled spells let you wipe all your sympathetic connections, so it isn't like they are sacrosanct.) As for Mind...<br /> <br /> Any Mage who is sufficiently good at Mind can wake up in the morning and decide to try out being gay that day. Or straight. Or a bigot, Or a member of this or that social group. Heck, it's a path to personal growth, if you think about it - walk a thousand miles in someone else's shoes, and all that.<br /> <br /> Their gender doesn't match their fleshy shell, and they don't have the Life to change it? Just change your gender. As far as you are concerned, the problem is solved. Prime might also be able to pull this off... maybe.<br /> <hr /><br /> Acanthus and Moros are kinda out of luck though (I dunno - maybe Fate could streamline the whole transitioning process with <i>amazing</i> luck. But I can't see a way to use Death or Matter in an appropriate way). But otherwise...<br /> <br /> Unlike the proverbial physician, Mages <i>can</i> heal themselves. So I'd assume that any Mage that didn't address the issue has a good reason for doing so.<br /> <br /> Now, the Hubris of doing so...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like those spins. Never thought of using Prime or Mind like that. (I'd favour using forces to set people on fire if they're clocking me but APPARENTLY that's 'hubristic' and 'excessive' and 'a breach of the veil')<br /> I mean the Space thing is just explicitly against RAW/RAI, but -shrug- that's been hashed over. To death. And back.<br /> <br /> mind though, 'a good reason for doing so' is a very big category. There's all the same reasons that a Sleeper who can pass as cis might choose not to go stealth - identity, community, solidarity - as well as magical reasons; it's something <i>someone</i> would have to upkeep, on a practical level, and for most people it's a strong part of who you are - so embracing it might well be a path to Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T02:39:52-07:00","id":618642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=618057#post618057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any Mage who is sufficiently good at Mind can wake up in the morning and decide to try out being gay that day. Or straight. Or a bigot, Or a member of this or that social group. Heck, it's a path to personal growth, if you think about it - walk a thousand miles in someone else's shoes, and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of Dave's blog posts actually noted this is totally a thing mages do. Mechanically, they use spells to give themselves Conditions, then resolve them for Beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T03:04:32-07:00","id":618650,"title":"","content":"All I would so is change the idea of the &quot;real name&quot; to that of the &quot;fallen name&quot;. It's the cattle brand of the fallen world, a bar code that states &quot;this is all you are and all you ever shall be&quot;. Another symbol of oppression placed upon you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T03:35:21-07:00","id":618661,"title":"","content":"I would like the idea of changing &quot;Real&quot; in to &quot;Fallen&quot; Name if True Name cannot change it function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T05:44:08-07:00","id":618699,"title":"","content":"(crossposting to Wyrd's name thread)<br /> <br /> I am considering changing it to &quot;sympathetic name,&quot; for the same reason. &quot;True&quot; names (apart from their use in literally *two* places in the whole gameline to designate the Archmastery Excision of Space) run counter to Awakening's magical thesis, where a mage's deliberately-constructed magical identity (their &quot;Shadow&quot; name) can be said to be <i>more</i> real than their Sleeper identity. There's room in Mage's cosmology for mages who argue that one's Fallen identity is inescapable, and it's the Seers of the Throne. Compare the Daksha (creepy as they are for other reasons) with the Chrysalides: the Pentacle Legacy is accepting of transformation, the Seer Legacy is based on dismorphia.<br /> <br /> I'm currently seeing if there's room for a bit more explanation of the topic in the corebook, as institutionally the Pentacle are ahead of Sleeper society when it comes to accepting transgendered, agendered, or similar. <i>Every single mage</i> has a deadname-equivalent, and referring to another mage by her sympathetic identity unless you're the most intimate of friends is incredibly rude at best and a punishable offence in most Silver Ladder, Guardian, and Free Council Caucuses. When your sex and gender are only three dots of Life and Mind away from being changed magically, when you appear in the Astral as your soul's self-image no matter what your physical body looks like, when mage society is founded on the notion of escaping from the oppressive systems of the Lie and defining yourself as a magical being, a woman insisting that she's a woman despite Sleepers' limited society saying otherwise is no big deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T05:45:34-07:00","id":618702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=618650#post618650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the cattle brand of the fallen world, a bar code that states &quot;this is all you are and all you ever shall be&quot;. Another symbol of oppression placed upon you.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T15:34:14-07:00","id":619514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=618699#post618699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When your sex and gender are only three dots of Life and Mind away from being changed magically</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I was wondering if changing your sex was going to be Patterning like in first edition or if it would be revised for Weaving. I see the goal of putting everything in line with the Practices continues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T15:40:09-07:00","id":619520,"title":"","content":"Turning a human into a different human is Weaving. Turning him into a fish is Patterning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T15:44:27-07:00","id":619521,"title":"","content":"Okay, so.<br /> <br /> I snuck a sidebar onto the end of the 2e core's Shadow Name section. I've tweaked its wording a few times in discussion with several trans friends:<br /> <br /> Shadow Names<br /> A Shadow Name is an expression of who the mage thinks she is in the Supernal World, without the Fallen, mundane person inside it. Most are only used when performing magic or meeting other mages, like a persona that can be adopted at will. Some mages change their voice or body language so much that at first glance they\u2019re unrecognizable when out of character.<br /> Mages take their Shadow Names very seriously. They\u2019re symbols, and therefore Supernal, influencing their bearers\u2019 lives. A mage naming himself after a god, for example, would be able to use items relating to his namesake as magical tools, but might find his magical career influenced to force him into that identity, events eerily paralleling the myth-symbols he made his magical identity from. Not every mage is reenacting her namesake\u2019s legend \u2014 not even most of them \u2014 but a Shadow Name is not something to be chosen lightly.<br /> A Shadow Name serves two functions. First, it helps conceal the mage\u2019s sympathetic name from enemy mages who might use that knowledge to cast spells on her sympathetically (see p. XX). More importantly, though, it prevents the mage\u2019s Nimbus from affecting those who only know her by her Sleeping identity. So long as the mage practices magic within her Shadow Name, only those things close to her as a mage (her cabal, sanctum, apprentices, dedicated tools, etc.) are affected by her Nimbus.<br /> A Shadow Name\u2019s protection works best, however, if a mage avoids using magic in the presence of the loved ones of his Sleeper life. If he allows too much of a connection to form between his Shadow Name and his un-Awakened family and friends they may yet fall under the influence of his magic.<br /> Using a mage\u2019s sympathetic name to address or refer to him except in the most intimate of friendships is considered offensively rude by the overwhelming majority of magical societies. In some Orders, such as the Free Council, Silver Ladder, and Guardians of the Veil, it\u2019s a punishable crime.<br /> [sidebar]<br /> <br /> Magical Identity Politics<br /> As a culture based around the rejection of mortal oppression who almost all construct new identities for magical purposes, the Awakened have always been more enlightened than Sleeping society with regard to acceptance of different genders and sexualities, even if they remain as sadly prone to other prejudices as Sleepers. Many mages appear as different sexes when in the Astral Realms, or use their spells and Legacies to become who they <i>are</i>, without the Lie\u2019s constraints. Many Mastigos and Thyrsus deliberately change gender, sex, and orientation temporarily as a means of self-examination and growth.<br /> Historically, Sleeping \u201cmagical\u201d practices were a haven for transgender and non-binary people in many cultures; modern mages know that these roles are sometimes just as limiting as outright persecution, but some older Legacies were formed around them and must contend with how their inheritance appears to the modern Orders.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T16:56:43-07:00","id":619561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=619521#post619521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so.<br /> <br /> I snuck a sidebar onto the end of the 2e core's Shadow Name section. I've tweaked its wording a few times in discussion with several trans friends:<br /> <br /> Shadow Names<br /> A Shadow Name is an expression of who the mage thinks she is in the Supernal World, without the Fallen, mundane person inside it. Most are only used when performing magic or meeting other mages, like a persona that can be adopted at will. Some mages change their voice or body language so much that at first glance they\u2019re unrecognizable when out of character.<br /> Mages take their Shadow Names very seriously. They\u2019re symbols, and therefore Supernal, influencing their bearers\u2019 lives. A mage naming himself after a god, for example, would be able to use items relating to his namesake as magical tools, but might find his magical career influenced to force him into that identity, events eerily paralleling the myth-symbols he made his magical identity from. Not every mage is reenacting her namesake\u2019s legend \u2014 not even most of them \u2014 but a Shadow Name is not something to be chosen lightly.<br /> A Shadow Name serves two functions. First, it helps conceal the mage\u2019s sympathetic name from enemy mages who might use that knowledge to cast spells on her sympathetically (see p. XX). More importantly, though, it prevents the mage\u2019s Nimbus from affecting those who only know her by her Sleeping identity. So long as the mage practices magic within her Shadow Name, only those things close to her as a mage (her cabal, sanctum, apprentices, dedicated tools, etc.) are affected by her Nimbus.<br /> A Shadow Name\u2019s protection works best, however, if a mage avoids using magic in the presence of the loved ones of his Sleeper life. If he allows too much of a connection to form between his Shadow Name and his un-Awakened family and friends they may yet fall under the influence of his magic.<br /> Using a mage\u2019s sympathetic name to address or refer to him except in the most intimate of friendships is considered offensively rude by the overwhelming majority of magical societies. In some Orders, such as the Free Council, Silver Ladder, and Guardians of the Veil, it\u2019s a punishable crime.<br /> [sidebar]<br /> <br /> Magical Identity Politics<br /> As a culture based around the rejection of mortal oppression who almost all construct new identities for magical purposes, the Awakened have always been more enlightened than Sleeping society with regard to acceptance of different genders and sexualities, even if they remain as sadly prone to other prejudices as Sleepers. Many mages appear as different sexes when in the Astral Realms, or use their spells and Legacies to become who they <i>are</i>, without the Lie\u2019s constraints. Many Mastigos and Thyrsus deliberately change gender, sex, and orientation temporarily as a means of self-examination and growth.<br /> Historically, Sleeping \u201cmagical\u201d practices were a haven for transgender and non-binary people in many cultures; modern mages know that these roles are sometimes just as limiting as outright persecution, but some older Legacies were formed around them and must contend with how their inheritance appears to the modern Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Looks good.<br /> <br /> I just have a couple of very minor points. First, a mage need not necessarily use his Sympathetic / Real Name as part of his &quot;Sleeping Identity.&quot; Just as mages can easily change sex and gender, their magic permits them to change minds and physical and electronic records, if for no other reason that to conceal their Sympathetic Name. I hope the text makes clear that mages have multiple identities / names, including their Shadow Name, Sympathetic Name, and one or more Sleeping Names / identities, that may or may not be the same as or related to their Sympathetic name. Something as simple as entries in the Lexicon section of the book might provide some clarity. <br /> <br /> Although I have no issue with a permanent and indelible Sympathetic Name, the sidebar doesn't really solve the concern some have expressed that, absent the intervention of an archmaster, a character has no control over their Sympathetic Name, as it may not reflect or even be opposed to their Fallen identity. My reading of the relevant forum threads was that people fully understood and have no objection to the nature and impact of a Shadow Name, but didn't like the implications of a Real Name that they couldn't change because of real world transgender discrimination issues. <br /> <br /> Lastly, can a mage change his Shadow Name, and is the magical tool use relating to the Shadow Name automatic or does it require a separate merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T17:34:26-07:00","id":619578,"title":"","content":"Now I've got this image of Norma Jeane Mortenson as a mage. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaveB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many Mastigos... deliberately change gender</div> </div> </div> </div> Now there's something I've never considered before...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T17:57:54-07:00","id":619588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=619561#post619561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looks good.<br /> <br /> I just have a couple of very minor points. First, a mage need not necessarily use his Sympathetic / Real Name as part of his &quot;Sleeping Identity.&quot; Just as mages can easily change sex and gender, their magic permits them to change minds and physical and electronic records, if for no other reason that to conceal their Sympathetic Name. I hope the text makes clear that mages have multiple identities / names, including their Shadow Name, Sympathetic Name, and one or more Sleeping Names / identities, that may or may not be the same as or related to their Sympathetic name. Something as simple as entries in the Lexicon section of the book might provide some clarity. <br /> <br /> Although I have no issue with a permanent and indelible Sympathetic Name, the sidebar doesn't really solve the concern some have expressed that, absent the intervention of an archmaster, a character has no control over their Sympathetic Name, as it may not reflect or even be opposed to their Fallen identity. My reading of the relevant forum threads was that people fully understood and have no objection to the nature and impact of a Shadow Name, but didn't like the implications of a Real Name that they couldn't change because of real world transgender discrimination issues. <br /> <br /> Lastly, can a mage change his Shadow Name, and is the magical tool use relating to the Shadow Name automatic or does it require a separate merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for anyone else, but I never had an issue with the fact that the Sympathetic Name can't be changed, just with the fact that it was the name given to the character at birth (which raises questions about characters whose names were changed before they were old enough to have a concept of identity), and the fave that it was called &quot;Real Name&quot; (which carries unfortunate implications about other names, Shadow or otherwise, being fake). Changing the title to &quot;Sympathetic Name&quot; resolves the latter issue for me, and the sidebar is ambiguous enough about what constitutes a Sympathetic Name that I'm not worried about the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-07-2015, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T18:27:39-07:00","id":619614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=619561#post619561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just have a couple of very minor points. First, a mage need not necessarily use his Sympathetic / Real Name as part of his Sleeping Identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but this is what the new identity merit is for,if that still exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T18:37:01-07:00","id":619626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=619614#post619614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but this is what the new identity merit is for,if that still exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's called Alternate Identity now, but yeah, it still exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T18:44:15-07:00","id":619642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=619588#post619588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never had an issue with the fact that the Sympathetic Name can't be changed, just with the fact that it was the name given to the character at birth (which raises questions about characters whose names were changed before they were old enough to have a concept of identity)</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Names,&quot; Imperial Mysteries OF</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cBecause my name isn\u2019t Helen.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know that\u2014\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLet me finish. I was five when Mom adopted me. I don\u2019t know why she changed my name, but I was too young. <b>Years of being called Helen outweighed a brief life I could barely remember.\u201d</b> A flicker of a smile crossed her lips. \u201cHaven\u2019t you wondered why I can\u2019t take an Apprentice? Pass on my Legacy?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI just assumed\u2026\u201d he said, his voice trailing into silence at her reaction.<br /> <br /> She shook her head.<br /> <br /> \u201cTo bond with a student, you have to exchange names. Real, sympathetic names. And I don\u2019t know what mine is. You\u2019ve never noticed because we grew up together. We Awakened together in the fire. You\u2019re my brother and I love you, but you don\u2019t know who I am. Anamika. \u2018One without a name.\u2019\u201d<br /> <br /> His voice, when he found it, was oddly hollow. \u201cAnd the archmasters know?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s so much about sympathy that we don\u2019t understand. Why isn\u2019t my name Helen? <b>We leave threads everywhere we go, with every interaction. We can sense, create, destroy and follow those threads, but we don\u2019t know what they\u2019re made of. We don\u2019t know why our first, oldest ones imprint so strongly.</b> I want to know. I need to know, and Mastery is not enough.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">characterlimit</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T19:03:15-07:00","id":619651,"title":"","content":"Dave, how hard is for a mage to change its shadow name? What does it entail?<br /> <br /> If you can't approach this here, or on the core book, would you consider it for Signs of Sorcery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T19:40:38-07:00","id":619689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=619642#post619642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me rephrase that. It raises and answers questions, and I dislike the canon answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T20:42:57-07:00","id":619710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=619689#post619689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me rephrase that. It raises and answers questions, and I dislike the canon answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then houserule it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T20:51:31-07:00","id":619723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=619710#post619710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then houserule it?</div> </div> </div> </div>To reiterate:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=619588#post619588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the sidebar is ambiguous enough about what constitutes a Sympathetic Name that I'm not worried about the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T21:13:07-07:00","id":619749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=619588#post619588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changing the title to &quot;Sympathetic Name&quot; resolves the latter issue for me, and the sidebar is ambiguous enough about what constitutes a Sympathetic Name that I'm not worried about the former.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I far as I can tell, the only thing about &quot;real / true names&quot; that changed is that they're now called &quot;sympathetic names,&quot; and Dave simply added the explanatory sidebar about &quot;shadow names&quot; to explain how it reflects a mage's true identity, not necessarily their sympathetic name, as well as emphasize how mages are generally more accepting of different genders and sexualities. <br /> <br /> A mage's sympathetic name is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=609282#post609282\">still his </a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=609282#post609282\">first identification in the Fallen, and it doesn't change</a>. As before, if a name was changed before a mage was old enough to have a concept of identity, their original name is still their sympathetic name. If you wish to change this, you may certainly do so, but it will require a houserule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T21:29:26-07:00","id":619754,"title":"","content":"It's like people aren't even reading my posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T04:28:57-07:00","id":619916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=619521#post619521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Historically, Sleeping \u201cmagical\u201d practices were a haven for transgender and non-binary people in many cultures; modern mages know that these roles are sometimes just as limiting as outright persecution, but some older Legacies were formed around them and must contend with how their inheritance appears to the modern Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does this mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T05:11:16-07:00","id":619926,"title":"","content":"That some Legacies are ruled by cis-genderism. Like, just for boys, no girls allowed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T07:19:58-07:00","id":619974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=619916#post619916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does this mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like this <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw on RPG.net</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>First edition had one Theosophic Legacy of mystical hermaprodites whose practices are portrayed as being more than a little out of touch with modern ideas (they're also massive racists), while one of the antagonist Legacies preys on bodily dismorphia. </b></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T08:03:03-07:00","id":620027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=619754#post619754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like people aren't even reading my posts.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, hey! This is the first time you're posting in this thread, isn't it? I haven't seen anything before from ya... *Cough*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T09:31:52-07:00","id":620174,"title":"","content":"What it means is that while there have been cultures that looked on people who we would consider to be transgender or non-binary in terms of &quot;great, you can be one of our shamans&quot; or similar, that doesn't exactly constitute an understanding or acceptance of those gender identities. Proscribing a role for people can be better than rendering them invisible or outright trying to destroy them or force conformity, but it probably still kind of sucked to be a transgendered person who <i>didn't want</i> to be a shaman. It might also refer to occasions of magical traditions based on adopting the idea of gender fluidities even if a person wasn't transgendered (similar to Ancient Greek ideas about sex between men that had nothing to do with homosexuality). When you get Legacies built around these things, they're going to clash with modern people who recognise the problematic details. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That some Legacies are ruled by cis-genderism. Like, just for boys, no girls allowed.</div> </div> </div> </div> While half-correct, this is not what the sidebar is discussing (it's also mistaken to frame the idea of gender exclusivity in terms of being restricted by cis-gender, not least because some gender exclusive groups have actually phrased things in terms of &quot;joining us means being whatever gender we are&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T10:03:59-07:00","id":620212,"title":"","content":"Dave, I really appreciate the name change, and that sidebar is great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T10:04:51-07:00","id":620214,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I kind of just tried to interpret without looking in the book, so my bad. And you're quite right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T10:18:52-07:00","id":620231,"title":"","content":"I like the awareness in that sidebar, but it's also kind of troubling to me, because it keeps reminding me of some of the unhappy details of the state of gay rights in modern Iran.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T15:53:05-07:00","id":621667,"title":"","content":"A WoD book bothering you by making you think deeper about something in the real world is probably a feature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T05:51:23-07:00","id":622084,"title":"","content":"To be clear, that wasn't me saying that I'm bothered by the book, just... those poor Iranian gay people. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T15:44:09-07:00","id":628057,"title":"","content":"Personally, were this issue to come up for me, i'd rule that you have to actually change your biological sex to make your new gender's name your real name for purposes of sympathetic magic. Yes I'm fully aware that it's not fair. but in my mind it's the act of permanently changing your body that is the act of will required to actually change your real name. Under this system, a pre-op woudl most liekly indeed refer to it as a &quot;sympathetic name&quot;<br /> <br /> For the non trans people, i'd simply say that changing your legal name through standard legal methods DOES change your real name. When you get married and take on your spouses name, that's a real name change for purposes of sympathetic magic. You don't need the maiden name. If you go through the effort to be recognized by your government as your new name, that's a change of real name. But entering the witness protection program wouldn't change your real name at all. Your new name in that case is a false name, created to hide yourself. there are benefits and drawbacks.<br /> <br /> If the fallen world records it as your primary identity (through government records, your ID, etc.) it is your real name for purposes of sympathetic magic. For it to work as a trans mage, you also have to get the fallen world to recognize your new gender. And that generally takes surgery.<br /> <br /> Yes, this means hacking government records is a pretty good way to get real names of mages. It still requires a heavily penalized skill roll. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd rule this way because it a) makes sense to me and b) makes it impossible to hide the &quot;real name&quot; completely, because it's a construct of the fallen world. The True Name ritual is the only fix for it, which blocks the name based sympathetic connection completely.<br /> <br /> If the real name for sympathetic magic is the birth name only, legal name changes will stymie attempts to get it too well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5815-zaphod77","user":"zaphod77","date":". 08-15-2015, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5815-zaphod77","name":"zaphod77","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T15:50:58-07:00","id":628084,"title":"","content":"What? Why on earth would a cis person be able to change their sympathetic name though legal processes and a trans person not be able to? That doesn't make any sense. Either everyone should be able to change their sympathetic name by changing their legal name or no one should be able to. Pick one and apply your rules consistently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T16:27:40-07:00","id":628107,"title":"","content":"I'm aware it's totally unfair, but that the unfairness is a part of the fallen world.<br /> <br /> The consistent standard is &quot;will it change everything related on the true mundane ID&quot;? If someone can get his real ID to read the desired gender, the process of changing the &quot;real name&quot; to the other gender works. if not, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> AS i said, the entire &quot;birth name is the real name&quot; thing just doesn't sit well with me. What about people who didn't have a birth name? It can happen. The only thing that is actually consistent is this...<br /> <br /> The name that people in general would recognize as your real name if they knew the truth is your real name. I'm well aware that standard is a bit unfair to certain people. but it's the only one i can think of that gives everyone a real name.<br /> <br /> To change your real name it must be intended as a change of your real name, and also be recognized by the fallen world as a change of identity. Sadly, trans people do still have trouble with the latter. Letting them change it with the help of surgery is a compromise. I know a lot of bigots will refuse to recognize even that. But it's not fair to lock them out of it forever.<br /> <br /> And last name changes that hide the birth name under that system are not equally available to both sexes, so that's inconsistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5815-zaphod77","user":"zaphod77","date":". 08-15-2015, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5815-zaphod77","name":"zaphod77","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T17:06:05-07:00","id":628141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zaphod77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=628107#post628107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AS i said, the entire &quot;birth name is the real name&quot; thing just doesn't sit well with me. What about people who didn't have a birth name? It can happen. The only thing that is actually consistent is this...</div> </div> </div> </div>Then their real name is going to be the first name they were consistently called by for a relevant period of time. It doesn't have to be the name they were given literally at birth, it is just the first name they had. If someone somehow went 20 years without being given a name (not even naming themselves) and then people suddenly started calling them Jack for a month or two their real name would become Jack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T17:27:16-07:00","id":628145,"title":"","content":"By that logic, wouldn't it be possible to alter your True Name by useing Mind magic to alter everyones memory of your own name, including your own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T18:11:25-07:00","id":628156,"title":"","content":"If changing of real name depend on changing official ID, you simply doesn't need a ridiculous rule about trans people having to underwent surgery. All the unfairness of the setting will be handled by the legal obstacles to do this to begin with. It is simply stupid to think that you need a more drastic step just to transit from male-name to female-name.<br /> <br /> To begin with, because what's a male name and a female name changes from place to place. It is a cultural thing. And second because the laws about naming people vary from place to place. Where I live, you can give whatever name you want to a children, and an adult can change her name to whatever, also, but only once. If Jack wants to become Jane, he can do so without any legal concern.<br /> <br /> And, well. The problem with equaling Real Name with Official ID is that to change ID isn't all that hard, even for a mortal. Fake IDs, legal double-standards or non-standards (what about an ID from a country that doesn't exist anymore? I know one personally), fake names that are far recognized... you have a lot of grey areas where you'll have problems with this interpretation anyway. More than people that went without a name for more than five years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T22:33:12-07:00","id":628233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zaphod77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=628107#post628107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware it's totally unfair, but that the unfairness is a part of the fallen world.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't an issue of unfairness, it's an issue of not making sense. If a cis woman changes her legal name from Susan to Taylor that gets to count as her sympathetic name, but if a trans man changes his legal name from Susan to Taylor it doesn't? Why?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zaphod77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=628107#post628107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The consistent standard is &quot;will it change everything related on the true mundane ID&quot;? If someone can get his real ID to read the desired gender, the process of changing the &quot;real name&quot; to the other gender works. if not, it doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's sympathetic <i>name</i>, not sympathetic <i>sex</i>. You can get your name legally changed to whatever you damn well please. If Prince could change his legal name to a symbol, a trans woman can sure as hell get her legal name changed to Stephanie, whether the law recognizes her as a woman or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zaphod77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=628107#post628107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AS i said, the entire &quot;birth name is the real name&quot; thing just doesn't sit well with me. What about people who didn't have a birth name? It can happen. The only thing that is actually consistent is this...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, fine, just make sure your house rule is consistent. If changing your legal name is all it takes, changing your legal name should be all it takes for anyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zaphod77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=628107#post628107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The name that people in general would recognize as your real name if they knew the truth is your real name. I'm well aware that standard is a bit unfair to certain people. but it's the only one i can think of that gives everyone a real name.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly do you mean by &quot;if they knew the truth&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zaphod77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=628107#post628107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To change your real name it must be intended as a change of your real name, and also be recognized by the fallen world as a change of identity. Sadly, trans people do still have trouble with the latter. Letting them change it with the help of surgery is a compromise. I know a lot of bigots will refuse to recognize even that. But it's not fair to lock them out of it forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing a legal name is actually very easy, no matter your gender. Passing as a different sex can be difficult for some people, but it doesn't always require surgery, and more importantly it has nothing at all to do with your name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zaphod77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=628107#post628107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And last name changes that hide the birth name under that system are not equally available to both sexes, so that's inconsistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they are. Anyone can get their last name legally changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-16-2015, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T05:56:19-08:00","id":1470217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609097-trans-mages?p=611840#post611840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what? To the Lower Depths with silk gloves. I will be fully honest in this post. If you feel that my grievances do not apply to you, then please don't reply saying you were offended and that I should check my privilege. Nobody is forcing you to read this.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Please stop turning the subtext of entertainment into major political issues.</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>There is a lot in this thread about trying to control other posters' opinion, how to conduct oneself about trans relations, and tone policing.<br /> <br /> Please leave the thread and take an infraction as a warning.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.ama